# Do natural disasters kill more people than a century ago?
subtitle: "Today disasters kill about 45,000 people a year. Guess the 1920s toll, then see why the risk per person fell by about 98 percent."
tags: ["earth","history","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Deadlier than ever?\" note \"1920s vs 2010s\""

## Do natural disasters kill more people than a century ago?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - 1920s
      - 2010s
    values:
      - [524, 45]
      - [266, 6]
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 800
    y_label: Deaths a year
    bar_colors: same
    label_size: 40
    box:
      x: 110
      'y': 190
      w: 700
      h: 430
    stage: 0
sources:
    - id: owid_dis
      title: Natural disasters
      authors: Hannah Ritchie, Pablo Rosado and Max Roser
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/natural-disasters
      finding: over the last century, disaster death rates have fallen by more than 90 %; in most recent years disasters kill 10,000–20,000 people, less than 0.1 % of global deaths
    - id: owid_dec
      title: 'Decadal average: annual number of deaths from disasters'
      authors: Our World in Data, from EM-DAT, CRED / UCLouvain
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/decadal-deaths-disasters-type
      finding: 'average deaths a year from all disasters: about 524,000 in the 1920s (droughts about 472,000) and about 45,000 in the 2010s (droughts about 2,000); 2004 alone about 246,000'
    - id: owid_pop
      title: Population
      authors: Our World in Data, from HYDE and UN World Population Prospects
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/population
      finding: world population averaged about 1.97 billion in the 1920s and 7.42 billion in the 2010s; deaths per million people a year about 266 then and about 6 now

    text tag_k "thousands" #2f6b8f x 700 y 590 font_size 52 hidden true
    text tag_m "per million people" #b5482e cites ["owid_pop","owid_dec"] x 640 y 590 font_size 52 hidden true
    path dline dashed #2f2b26 cites ["owid_dec"] points [[-0.45,472],[0.45,472]] data true style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    text dlab "droughts" #2f2b26 at.data [0,400] font_size 44 hidden true
    text y2004 "2004 alone: ≈ 250k" #5e584e at.data [1,300] cites ["owid_dec"] font_size 46 hidden true
    text share "< 0.1% of deaths" #2f6b8f at.data [1,200] cites ["owid_dis"] font_size 46 hidden true

    card title "Are disasters deadlier than they used to be?"

Earthquakes, floods, storms, droughts: do they kill more people today than a hundred years ago?
    draw axes

In the 2010s, disasters killed about forty-five thousand people a year.
    draw bar_2 tag_k

    ask "Drag the 1920s bar to your guess." on bar_1 store g default "60" relative true tolerance 0.25
        right: Close: you said {g} thousand a year, and it was about {g.true} thousand.
        wrong: You said {g} thousand; it was about {g.true} thousand a year, more than ten times today's toll.

Most of it was drought, which in poor farming countries meant famine.
    draw dline dlab

Drought deaths fell from about four hundred and seventy thousand a year to about two thousand, as farming, trade and food aid improved.
    highlight bar_2

    erase dline dlab

Bad years still come: in 2004 alone, disasters killed (@draw y2004@) about a quarter of a million people, most of them in the Indian Ocean tsunami.

    erase y2004

    erase tag_k

And there were only two billion people then, (@draw tag_m@) against seven and a half billion now. So count per million people.

Two hundred and sixty-six deaths per million people a year, down to about six.
    animate stage 1 duration 3

A fall of about ninety-eight percent.
    text drop "−98%" #b5482e at.data [1,380] cites ["owid_dec","owid_pop"] font_size 80

Today disasters cause less than a tenth of one percent of all deaths in most years.
    draw share

So disasters still fill the news, but the chance of dying in one has never been smaller.
    highlight bar_2

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon storm size 300 set twemoji x 260 y 440 icon_look picture of tornado hidden true
    text q "Deadlier?" #b5482e x 680 y 500 font_size 110 hidden true
    text yrs "1920s vs 2010s" #2f2b26 x 680 y 360 font_size 64 hidden true
    thumb band "A century of disasters" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    text q "?" #b5482e x 300 y 400 font_size 260 hidden true
    text l1 "1920s" #2f2b26 x 300 y 660 font_size 72 hidden true
    shape b2 #2f6b8f shape rect x 680 y 320 width 220 height 40 style.fill #cfe3ee hidden true
    text v2 "45k a year" #2f6b8f x 680 y 400 font_size 64 hidden true
    text l2 "2010s" #2f2b26 x 680 y 660 font_size 72 hidden true
    thumb band "Drag the bar" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon earth size 260 set twemoji x 250 y 450 icon_look picture of "globe showing americas" hidden true
    text x4 "×4 people" #2f6b8f x 680 y 480 font_size 90 hidden true
    text deaths "deaths ×?" #b5482e x 680 y 350 font_size 90 hidden true
    thumb band "Guess first" kind band hidden true
    thumb st "Then vs now" kind stamp x 700 y 640 angle 5 hidden true
